<title>UK: LIFFE commodity turnover rises in October.</title>
<headline>LIFFE commodity turnover rises in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover in commodity futures and options traded on the London International Financial Futures Exchange (LIFFE) rose by 18,455 lots to 307,619 in October from the previous month, a LIFFE report showed.</p>
<p>Cocoa showed the biggest rise in the month -- futures increased to 119,303 from 101,723 lots in September while options rose to 4,148 contracts from 1,850 -- followed by increases in robusta coffee and wheat futures.</p>
<p>The total volume was slightly behind the year-ago period, but the cumulative Jan-Oct total of 3.311 million lots was above the 3.242 million recorded in the Jan-Oct period of 1995.</p>
<p>The year-to-date change in the total volume was an increase of two percent.</p>
<p>Volume details included,</p>
<p>		    Oct 96   Sept 96   Oct 95  Jan-Oct 96 Jan-Oct 95</p>
<p>TOTAL	     307,619  289,164   315,479  3,311,607  3,242,550</p>
<p>Cocoa futures   119,303  101,723   133,329  1,455,859  1,434,603</p>
<p>Coffee futures   99,647   83,474    95,426   990,638     876,599</p>
<p>No 5 Sugar fut   45,377   63,755    47,380   501,423     492,941</p>
<p>Wheat futures    14,490   12,097    10,018   100,121	79,300</p>
<p>BIFFEX		6,597    7,996     8,122    49,123	61,843</p>
<p>Cocoa options     4,148    1,850	 803    50,319	45,935</p>
<p>Coffee options   11,517   11,826    12,731    109,008    147,467</p>
<p>No 5 Sugar opt    1,955    1,090     1,792     11,560     21,107</p>
<p>Wheat options     1,467    1,647     1,357	7,889	9,942</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
